```
[CRITICAL] Telegram MarkdownV2 escaping is applied to already-escaped text, causing double-escaping and parse failures
File: /Users/robinsonchan/seatsniper/src/notifications/telegram/telegram.formatter.ts:49-54
```

In `formatListing`, the string template at lines 50-53 already contains manual escape sequences (e.g., `\\.`, `\\(`, `\\)`). This string is then passed to `this.escapeMarkdown()` which escapes ALL special characters again. The backslashes from the manual escapes get re-escaped, resulting in `\\\\(` instead of `\\(`. Every Telegram `sendMessage` call will fail with "Bad Request: can't parse entities" because the MarkdownV2 is malformed.

```typescript
// CURRENT (lines 49-54):
const details = this.escapeMarkdown(
  `${listing.rank}\\. ${platformBadge} Section ${listing.section}, Row ${listing.row}\n` +
  `   💰 $${listing.pricePerTicket}/ticket \\(${listing.quantity} avail\\)\n` +
  `   ${scoreEmoji} Value Score: ${listing.valueScore}/100\n` +
  `   📊 ${listing.recommendation}`
);

// FIX: Either escape manually OR use escapeMarkdown -- not both.
// Option A: Use escapeMarkdown on raw text (remove manual escapes):
const details = this.escapeMarkdown(
  `${listing.rank}. ${platformBadge} Section ${listing.section}, Row ${listing.row}\n` +
  `   💰 $${listing.pricePerTicket}/ticket (${listing.quantity} avail)\n` +
  `   ${scoreEmoji} Value Score: ${listing.valueScore}/100\n` +
  `   📊 ${listing.recommendation}`
);
```

The same double-escaping problem also exists in `formatFooter` (line 68) and `formatCompact` (line 139), where manually escaped `\\.` and `\\|` are passed into `escapeMarkdown()`.

