```
[HIGH] Seat map image files are missing -- all generateHighlightedMap calls will fail silently
File: /Users/robinsonchan/seatsniper/src/venues/seat-map.service.ts:155
```

The `assetsPath` at line 35 points to `../../assets/seat-maps` relative to the compiled output. The actual directory `/Users/robinsonchan/seatsniper/assets/seat-maps/` only contains README files, not any actual `.jpg` images (moda-center.jpg, climate-pledge-arena.jpg, etc.) referenced in the registry. Every call to `sharp(imagePath)` will throw a file-not-found error. While the service catches this and returns `null`, it means the seat map feature is completely non-functional without any compile-time or startup-time warning.

A startup validation check should be added:
```typescript
// In constructor or an init method:
for (const [, venue] of this.registry) {
  const imagePath = path.join(this.assetsPath, venue.imageFile);
  if (!fs.existsSync(imagePath)) {
    logger.warn(`[SeatMap] Missing image file: ${imagePath} for venue ${venue.venueName}`);
