[MEDIUM] Telegram formatter escapeMarkdown regex is incorrect -- it escapes the hyphen wrong
File: /Users/robinsonchan/seatsniper/src/notifications/telegram/telegram.formatter.ts:126
```

The regex `/[_*[\]()~`>#+=|{}.!\\-]/g` places the hyphen `-` at the end of the character class preceded by `\\`. Depending on the JS engine, `\\-` inside a character class may be interpreted as a range from `\` to nothing, or may work but is fragile. Additionally, the Telegram MarkdownV2 spec requires escaping the characters `_`, `*`, `[`, `]`, `(`, `)`, `~`, `` ` ``, `>`, `#`, `+`, `-`, `=`, `|`, `{`, `}`, `.`, `!`. The current regex also escapes `\` itself, which would cause issues if the input already has intentional escapes.

```typescript
// FIX: Place hyphen at the start or properly escape it:
escapeMarkdown(text: string): string {
  return text.replace(/([_*\[\]()~`>#+=|{}.!\-\\])/g, '\\$1');
}
```

